+# Rule Review UI (Next.js)
+
+A runnable single-page app for analysts to review a `/evaluate` response.
+No UI-library or Tailwind dependency — styling uses Next.js built-in styled-jsx.
+
+## Run it (Windows)
+
+Requires **Node 20.9** — https://nodejs.org/download/release/v20.9.0/
+
+```powershell
+node --version         # -> v20.9.x
+
+cd ui
+npm install
+npm run dev            # http://localhost:3000
+```
+
+Start the backend API in another terminal (CORS is enabled for dev):
+
+```powershell
+# from the project root, with the .venv activated (see main README)
+rule-engine-api        # or: uvicorn rule_engine.api.app:app --reload
+```
+
+Open http://localhost:3000, edit the payload, click **Evaluate**.
+The UI reads the API URL from `ui\.env.local`
+(`NEXT_PUBLIC_RULE_ENGINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000`).
+
+> macOS / Linux: identical `npm` commands.
+
+## Files
+
+| File | What it is |
+|------|------------|
+| `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `next.config.mjs` | Minimal Next.js app (demo host) |
+| `app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx` | Demo page: enter a payload, call the API, render |
+| **`components/RuleReview/`** | **The reusable component (this is the portable part)** |
+
+## The reusable component
+
+`components/RuleReview/` is self-contained and **React-only** — no Tailwind, no
+CSS-in-JS library, no Next.js APIs. The single input is the API response.
+
+```
+components/RuleReview/
+├── index.ts         # exports { RuleReview } + all types
+├── RuleReview.tsx   # the component (table + hierarchy views)
+├── styles.ts        # scoped stylesheet (injected once, namespaced .re-root)
+└── types.ts         # TypeScript types for the API response
+```
+
+```tsx
+import { RuleReview } from "@/components/RuleReview";
+import type { EvaluationResponse } from "@/components/RuleReview";
+
+<RuleReview data={apiResponse} />
+<RuleReview data={apiResponse} defaultView="tree" />   // optional
+```
+
+### Moving it to another project
+
+Copy the whole **`components/RuleReview/`** folder in. That's it — it works in
+any React app (Next.js, Vite, CRA). It needs only `react`
+(`useState`/`useEffect`). Styles auto-inject on first render.
+
+## API base URL
+
+Set in `.env.local` (already created):
+
+```bash
+NEXT_PUBLIC_RULE_ENGINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
+```
+
+In production, lock down CORS on the API side:
+
+```bash
+RULE_ENGINE_CORS_ORIGINS="https://analyst.example.com" rule-engine-api
+```
+
+## What the analyst sees
+
+- **Overall decision** banner (PASS / FAIL).
+- Per exception code: a card with **summary counts** (total / passed / blocking /
+  warnings / errors), a highlighted **blocking failures** list, and a **rules
+  table** (status, rule, severity, the check, and the detail/reason).
+- A **"failures & warnings only"** toggle to cut noise.
+- Status shown with icon **and** label **and** colour (not colour alone).
+
+Each card has a **Table / Hierarchy** switch:
+- **Table** — flat list of every leaf rule (good for scanning/filtering).
+- **Hierarchy** — the nested AND/OR/NOT tree, expandable from the root. Branches
+  containing a failure or warning open automatically; fully-passing branches
+  start collapsed so attention goes to what matters.
